# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Tool caches
.pytest_cache/

# uv writes .venv/.gitignore containing "*", so the venv already self-ignores.
# Listed anyway -- explicit beats relying on another tool's internals.
.venv/

# Streamlit: config.toml IS COMMITTED (Sprint 6 needs the dark theme there).
# Only secrets are ignored.
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED -- do not "tidy" these in later:
#   uv.lock          Railway builds with `uv sync --locked --no-dev
#                    --no-install-project` and fails without it. Two
#                    consequences worth knowing: --no-dev means pytest is NOT
#                    in the image (intended), and --no-install-project means
#                    the project is NOT installed as a package -- tax.py and
#                    engine.py import only because `streamlit run` puts the
#                    script's directory on sys.path. P3a proves that in the
#                    container rather than leaving it to Sprint 6 to discover.
#                    --locked also means: hand-edit pyproject.toml without
#                    re-running uv lock and the BUILD fails, not the app.
#   railway.toml     Start command, healthcheck, restart policy. Config-as-code
#                    overrides the dashboard, so this file wins.
#   cube.json        Sprint 9 requires it committed; the app must not compute it
#   .python-version  uv and Railpack both read it

# Tests
tests/results_*.txt